1. BOARD P'S EXISTING PROTECTION WITH ITS FETS WELDED
   the gauge's OCD1, OCD2 (20 A 2 s, 24 A 1 s)    firmware levels acting through Q1 and Q2: none: Q1 and Q2 are welded
   the AFE's AOLD, ASCD (30 A, 55.6 A)            comparators set from data flash, acting through Q1 and Q2: none: Q1 and Q2 are welded
   the second level U2 (BQ7720700)                cell voltage, open wire and temperature; no current input: none on current
   F2's heater (SCF9550)                          fired by U2's COUT or the gauge's FUSE output (firmware): none on current without firmware
   F2's element (30 A)                            100 % holds 1 h at least; 200 % opens within 60 s: no opening assured under 60.00 A
   the 25 A MINI blades F1 (board P), F3 (board E) 110 % holds 360000 s at least; 135 % opens within 600 s: no opening assured under 33.75 A
   the lowest current any of them opens on its own is 33.75 A, over the battery FETs' 150 C current below: none meets the
   criterion, so a minimal addition is designed (section 3)

2. THE LIMITING SERIES PART THE ELEMENT WAS SIZED AGAINST: Q39/Q40, THE CHARGER'S BATTERY FET PAIR ON BOARD A AS L4-E11 DRAFTED IT UNTIL ITS ROUND 9
   RDS(on) 21.136 mOhm each: L4-E11's bound at a 150 C junction from the sheet's printed maxima (the actual is lower at a lower junction)
   installed (Zself + Zmut) 33.12 K/W steady: E11-29's TARGET then (withdrawn in L4-E11's 19c), not a measurement; with both FETs at the bound the even split
   gives each FET the largest loss (SLVA673A 2.4 for enhanced FETs; a lower RDS(on) in one FET lowers its loss)
   150 C held at 21.38 A from the +70 C line and 20.53 A from 76.25 C (L4-E12's E5 dwell without the hold), FETs only: DERIVED, not a rating
   its uncertainty is the installed path's: with it 20 % lower, as targeted, 20 % higher:
     x0.8: 23.90 A (+70 C), 22.95 A (76.25 C); x1.0: 21.38 A (+70 C), 20.53 A (76.25 C); x1.2: 19.52 A (+70 C), 18.74 A (76.25 C)
   the exposure a trip at the cells' 24 A would leave, held: 22.00 A: TJ 154.7 C (+70 C), 161.0 C (76.25 C); 23.00 A: TJ 162.6 C (+70 C), 168.8 C (76.25 C); 24.00 A: TJ 170.8 C (+70 C), 177.1 C (76.25 C)
   so 'at or under 24 A' is not a protection criterion; the criterion is current AND time for every part (section 5)
   since L4-E11's round 9 its draft carries Q39, Q40 and Q42 (section 4's selection, drafted, not applied) and E11-29 is section 4's junction limit;
   the figures above are the pair's, kept as the basis the criterion and the element were derived on

3. THE SELECTED ELEMENT: AN LM5069 BREAKER ON BOARD P (THE -1, LATCH-OFF: 3b), FROM Q2'S SOURCE TO PACK_P, ENABLED BY A MAKE-LAST DOCK LOOP
   the family board E's U6 already uses (its -2, LCSC C111822; the -1's code is Layer 6's to file, the same VSSOP-10 land) and the FET board A's PA
   stage already uses (LCSC C2876544): no new part family
   sense RS: 4 and 7.5 mOhm in parallel = 2.6087 mOhm, 1 % and 50 ppm/K over 100 K: +-1.5 % (the parts only; the traces and Kelvin taps are E-9's)
     its window: 2.6015 to 2.6546 mOhm (the largest limit at most the cells' 24 A, the least above the 18 A service)
     current limit 18.32 / 21.08 / 23.93 A (VCL 48.5 to 61.5 mV over TJ -40 to 125 C, printed at VIN 48 V); breaker 30.21 to 50.59 A (VCB 80 to 130 mV)
     the limits are printed at VIN 48 V and used at 10.6 to 16.8 V (Q-TI-L9S-1, E-2, E-3, E-9); the shares: 4 mOhm 65.2 %; 7.5 mOhm 34.8 %
   power limit: RPWR 8450 ohm (equation 9 at VSNS 5 mV and 16.8 V, the next E96 value up): 32.52 W nominal, VSNS 5.05 mV
     its spread: 24.71 to 40.32 W with the table's 19/25/31 mV read as a ratio (the table prints it at 25 mV only); read as an offset, 71.16 W
     without the power limit the FET would see 402.1 W (VIN x the largest limit): the limit is relied on (E-2, Q-TI-L9S-1)
   fault timer: 10 nF (+-10 %): 0.282 to 0.897 ms (VTMRH 3.76 to 4.16 V, 51 to 120 uA); insertion 4.23 to 15.25 ms (3 to 8 uA)
   gate: 690 nC to remove (2 x 153 nC at 10 V scaled to 12.6 V, and the dv/dt capacitor's swing); breaker release 16.5 us (tCB 1.2 us, 45 mA);
     after the timer or the enable's opening 395 us (1.75 mA): clearing 1.292 ms at most from the limit's onset (tCL 45 us typical, no maximum printed)
   dv/dt start: 22 nF (+-10 %) into 593 uF (VSYS's 489 uF, CELL_FUSED's 104 uF), gate 10 to 22 uA: inrush 0.659 A at most, 40.7 ms at most
     SLVA673A 3.2.2.7: 11.1 W for 20.3 ms equivalent, under the power limit's least 24.7 W, so the timer never runs
   the -2's timer ratio: 1.33 % at most, conservative: it pairs the slowest fault current (on) with the fastest sink (off) (0.5 % typical); its dwell 0.222 s at most (3b judges its whole cycle)
   FETs: 2 x CSD18510Q5B (40 V, VGS +-20 V, 0.96 mOhm at 10 V, IDM 400 A, junction 150 C, RthJA 50 C/W on 1 in2 2 oz, 125 on its least pad, RthJC 0.8 C/W)
     held at 23.93 A: 0.247 W each at 1.728 mOhm (Figure 8's x1.8 at 150 C); case 101.0 C with both losses through one pad, junction 101.2 C
     the case used for the derating 103.0 C, factor 0.376 (equation 5): the first revision's retry estimate, kept as a bound over the held 101.0 C
     SOA at 16.8 V and 25 C (Figure 10 read at 300 dpi, +-10 %): DC 50 W; 10 ms 96 W; 1 ms 206 W; 100 us 1692 W; 10 us 4101 W
     the fault pulse: 40.32 W for 1.292 ms against 71.1 W derated: 0.57 (TI asks 0.67 at most); 1.00 with the offset reading
     the start: 11.1 W for 20.3 ms against 19.0 W derated (the DC line: no extrapolation past 10 ms): 0.58
     with Figure 10 read 10 % high (the SOA 10 % lower): 0.63 and 0.65; TI's margin holds up to an installed RthJA of 52.5 C/W per FET
     the 10 us line at 16.8 V: 244.1 A at 25 C; IDM 400 A against the breaker's 50.59 A (SLVA673A 3.1.2.2)
   input clamp: SMCJ18A on VIN (VR 18 V, VBR 20 V least, VC 29.2 V at 51.4 A), the part on board A's VBAT; output: board P's D1 (SMBJ20A)
     carries the lead's freewheel when the gate turns off (LM5069 11.1.2 B): on I2t, its 100 A for 8.3 ms half-sine is 41.5 A2s; the freewheel
     decays with the loop's L/R (not held), so at the pack's 480 A prospective it is within it for an L/R up to 0.36 ms (12.6 uH in that loop)
     VIN to SENSE's 0.3 V maximum is passed above 116.8 A, which only a hot short reaches before the gate is low (Q-TI-L9S-1, E-3)
   controller: VIN 9 to 80 V recommended, on from 9 V at most; the pack 10.6 to 16.8 V; OVLO to ground; UVLO from VIN through the enable
   the charge direction: the LM5069 limits no reverse current; a charge passes the FETs' channel while the breaker is on and their body
     diodes while it is off (VIN under POREN, or the enable open): the gauge's 1 A precharge in one diode 1.00 W (VSD 1 V at most), TJ 126.2 C
   not taken:
     - a limit whose largest is the pair's 20.53 A: its least 15.71 A falls under the 18 A service
     - a blade opening under the pair's current: at most 15.21 A, and the service at 118 % of it lies between the row that holds and the row that opens
     - for docking, an inrush element at board A's dock entry: the pre-charge pin J_PRE1 (10 ohm into 593 uF, a 5.93 ms time constant) needs a lead of 12.4 ms over the power pins to keep the step under the breaker's least threshold and 4.3 ms to keep VIN to SENSE under 0.3 V, and a hand sets the lead; a series element in the 23.93 A path heats beside the battery FETs, whose junction is the binding limit
     - the pair kept at (Zself + Zmut) at most 20.39 K/W with R17 apart: 38 % under E11-29's former 33.12 K/W, which L4-E11 judged of the order a board pour gives; it stays the fallback if E11-37 refuses three FETs
     - a single-wire enable to board A's ground: a short to ground, the commonest harness fault, would enable the breaker unseen (C2)
     - no RC hold: a reversed mating order of 1.88 ms would bring B-P1 back (C1)
     - a controller with a tighter limit tolerance now: the LM5066I of SLVA673A's examples, its sheet not held; it is E-5's fallback
     - for B-R1, one criterion at the SOA itself (under 1 with the reading) instead of the inhibit: it would accept the -1's hot restart at 0.95 but leave 5 % against a power limit whose spread at 5 mV is not printed (E-2)

3a. B-P1: DOCKING. Without a correction the breaker is on when the dock's power pins mate, so a docking reaches E11-30's 242.9 A:
     VIN to SENSE 0.634 V against the 0.3 V maximum; the 10 us line at 16.8 V derated to the 103.0 C case is 91.8 A (2.64 x over it), at a 75 C case 1.66 x
   C-1b SELECTED: a make-last enable loop into UVLO (LM5069 11.1.1 and Figure 45), with an RC hold. The loop leaves board P from VIN through
     10 kOhm on one J_SMB contact, crosses the dock on two contacts 1 mm short of the power pins, passes board A's chip PTC beside the battery
     FETs (the thermal guard, section 4) and returns on a second J_SMB contact, a ground contact between the two, to a 22 kOhm divider on the
     first 2N7002's gate; that FET holds the second's gate low, and the second, when on, pulls UVLO itself. The hold: R_U 200 kOhm from VIN
     charges C_U 3.3 uF on a node H, which reaches UVLO through 150 ohm and a 1N4148W, against the 12 to 30 uA hysteresis sink (at 10.6 V H
     settles at 4.6 V, over 2.55 V and the diode's 0.715 V); when the second inverter pulls UVLO, C_U drains behind it through 150 ohm and the diode
     (107 mA at most: 0.11 of its 1 A 1 ms surge, 0.71 of its 150 mA average rating), so the turn-off no longer waits for C_U
   the timing: the insertion time runs only when VIN passes PORIT, so it applies to a start by the gauge's own FET (4.23 to 15.25 ms), not to a
     docking; on the enable the LM5069 raises the gate UVLODEL (55 us typical, no maximum printed) after UVLO passes 2.45 to 2.55 V, which the RC
     hold makes 0.110 to 0.907 s after the enable mates; then a dv/dt start at 0.659 A at most, VIN to SENSE 1.72 mV
     without the hold a power pin mating 1.88 ms late meets OUT at 2.09 V (the dv/dt rate 1.111 V/ms): the breaker's least 30.21 A through the loop;
     with it a reversed order up to 111.6 ms is tolerated (condition C1)
   undocking: the loop opens; the first inverter is off in 2.5 us, the second on in 16.0 us and UVLO falls at once, the gate low 395 us later
     (UVLODEL 11 us typical, no maximum printed): 0.41 ms in all, before the pins part at a withdrawal under 2.42 m/s (through C_U it took 1.51 ms,
     0.66 m/s); C_U drains in 1.10 ms behind it. Any open is off (fail-safe); a short to ground on either loop
     conductor holds it off (condition C2). The gauge's own FET turning on is a start too: E11-30's waveform no longer arises
   the alternative, an inrush element at board A's dock entry, is not taken (the not-taken list above): the pre-charge pin's lead time is the hand's

3b. THE RETRY: THE -2'S REPEATED WAVEFORM AGAINST EVERY PROTECTED PART, AND THE -1 (LM5069 sections 5 and 8.4.3)
   the sheet: the -1 latches off on a fault, the -2 retries; on the -2 the TIMER cycles seven times between its restart threshold (1.187 to 1.313 V)
     and VTMRH (3.76 to 4.16 V) after the fault time, the
     gate turns on at 0.3 V on the eighth fall, and the fault time and the restart repeat while the fault remains
   one cycle with C_T at 10 nF +-10 %: on (the fault time from 0.3 V, then the gate's turn-off) 1.076 to 1.227 ms; off 50.7 to 62.0 ms (the shortest from the
     largest sink current); a ramp ahead of it while the load lets the output rise, at 0.413 to 1.111 V/ms
   the series current per cycle is never over the largest limit, 23.93 A, nor over the power limit over VDS: through the slowest ramp and the
     limited phase at most 5.14 A2s and 0.351 As; over the cycle at most 55.6 A2 on average, 7.46 A RMS, 0.097 of the held 23.93 A's heating
   the breaker FET: a hard short 43.4 mJ a cycle, 0.84 W, case 118.1 C, 0.79 of the derated SOA (0.88 with the reading); a resistive fault on VSYS
     at 0.915 ohm (just over the least limit at full voltage) loads the ramp: 174 mJ a cycle (130 in 5.6 ms of ramp), 3.03 W, case 228 C
   per part through a persistent fault on the -2, settled from 76.25 C (energy a cycle | average | settled | limit | verdict):
     board P's Q1/Q2, enhanced (each) | 6.4 mJ | 0.069 W | TJ 83.2 C (both losses through one pad) | 150 C | within
     board P's Q1 under BAT-F20 (its body diode) | 351 mJ | 3.80 W | TJ 266 C | 150 C (1.48 W on its pad) | OVER: DD-5, as in the held and service rows
     the three battery FETs (each) | 12.1 mJ | 0.131 W | TJ 83.4 C | 150 C | within
     R17 (5 W) | 25.7 mJ | 0.278 W | - | 5 W | within (derating NOT HELD, E-6)
     R10 (2 W) | 10.3 mJ | 0.111 W | - | 2 W | within (E-6)
     the breaker's sense | 13.4 mJ | 0.145 W | - | 2 W each (a requirement) | within
     the XT60 (30 A) | - | 7.46 A RMS, 23.93 A peak | - | 30 A | within
     the dock contacts (4 x 9 A) | - | 1.86 A RMS a pin at an even split | - | 9 A | within (E-4)
     the pack path's copper | - | - | 0.89 K over the air | 10 K | within
     the barrel field | - | - | 0.74 K | 10 K | within
     the 25 A blades and F2 | - | 7.46 A RMS | - | 25 A, 30 A | within (E-7)
     the Keystone 3568 holder | - | 7.46 A RMS | - | no rating printed | NOT HELD: DD-4
     the cells | - | 7.46 A RMS | - | 24 A | within
     the enable loop's parts (2N7002s, PTC, R_U, C_U) | 0 | the loop's static 0.45 mA | - | - | not cycled by the -2's restart (internal)
     the breaker FET, a hard short | 43.4 mJ | 0.84 W | case 118.1 C | SOA with TI's margin 0.67 | OVER TI's margin: 0.79 (0.88 with the reading)
     the breaker FET, a resistive fault on VSYS (0.915 ohm) | 174 mJ (130 in the ramp) | 3.03 W | case 228 C | 150 C | OVER
   so the -2 does NOT meet the criterion: its repeated waveform takes the breaker FET past TI's margin in a hard short and past 150 C in a
     resistive fault on VSYS; every other protected part settles under its held reading (section 4), Q1 under BAT-F20 excepted (DD-5)
   the -1 against the service and the recovery: the 10 A and the 18 A never reach the least limit, so neither variant trips in the service;
     after a fault the -1 stays off: on battery the kit goes dark, as CONOPS 4e already states for the over-current backstop ("recovers only on
     an input") and POWER-THERMAL 9.3 takes as the safe state ("restarting into the same load would repeat it"); recovery by redocking (the loop
     pulls UVLO low), by an input's return (DD-7) and by the thermal guard's own cycle; the timer falls under 0.3 V in 34.0 ms at most
   which UVLO edge: the sheet asks the timer under 0.3 V for a restart and does not say at which edge; read at the falling edge, a pulse within
     34.0 ms of a latch does not restart, which fails safe (the breaker stays off; a later pulse or a redocking restarts it); read at the rising
     edge, the RC hold's least 0.110 s covers it
   IF-1 is now critical to the service: under the -1 a start that meets the power limit runs the timer and latches the breaker, and the start
     leaves room for at most 0.81 A of load at full VDS (the power limit's least less the inrush's 11.1 W); L4-E11 owns the hold-off
   a fault just under a unit's limit and over the service (held, never tripping, either variant): every part at its held reading (section 4);
     the battery FETs bounded by the thermal guard, which trips and restarts at the PTC's rate only for loads IF-1 holds off; a resistive
     fault on VSYS, which IF-1 cannot hold off, latches the -1 at the guard's first restart; Q1 under BAT-F20 OVER (DD-5)
   SELECTED: the -1 (latch-off). Every protected part then meets one fault event, at the per-cycle energy above, with no accumulation
   one start into the worst resistive fault on VSYS (either variant's first event, 0.915 ohm): 180 mJ, equivalent 40.32 W for 4.46 ms (SLVA673A
     equation 7): 0.54 of the derated SOA from the inside air (TI's start basis, 0.60 with the reading); hot it is 0.82 at the held 101.0 C
     and 0.85 at 103.0 C, past the 1.5x margin the -2 was rejected on; hot restarts are credible (the guard's cycle, DD-7's pulse, a quick redock)
   B-R1, ONE CRITERION FOR BOTH VARIANTS: TI's 1.5x margin over the derated SOA for every event at the case it can occur at. The -2 fails it
     (0.79 in a hard short; 228 C in a resistive fault). The -1 meets it only if a restart happens at a case of 89.9 C at most (83.2 C with
     the reading allowance)
   C-1c SELECTED: a restart inhibit on the breaker pad. An NTC (Murata NXRT15XH103FA1B, 10 kOhm +-1 %, B25/85 3434 K, B +-1 %) in a
     ratiometric bridge from VIN (150 kOhm over it; 0.111 mA at most against its 0.12 mA) drives a comparator that pulls UVLO, gated so that it
     acts only while PGD is low (the breaker off, starting or in a fault: VDS over 1.62 to 3.4 V), never on a running breaker. Window: allow
     from 77.25 C (the inside air plus 1 K), block from 83.20 C; trip 80.22 C +-2.97 K: the NTC takes +-1.02 K (R 0.36, B 0.65, the B
     tolerance taken as printed at 25/50), leaving +-1.95 K for the comparator (1.59 mV of offset is 0.5 K at 0.116 V), the bridge, the
     hysteresis and the pad's gradient (E-15); its NTC at the trip 1653 ohm
     the worst resistive start: 0.54 from the air, 0.57 at the trip (0.64 with the reading), 0.60 at the block edge (0.67 with the reading)
     a fault while hot: PGD low lets the inhibit pull UVLO, which the -1 does not latch; it restarts when the pad cools under the trip, so any
     further event starts at 83.2 C at most; a quick redock or DD-7's pulse after heavy use waits for the pad to cool (its time NOT HELD, E-15)

4. B-P2: THE BATTERY FETS' JUNCTION LIMIT AND EVERY SERIES PART AT THE BREAKER'S LARGEST LIMIT, 23.93 A, FROM 76.25 C
   the limit: the hottest battery FET's junction at most 150 C held at 23.93 A from 76.25 C, the band carrying the current (9.16 K: 1 oz 9.16, 2 oz 9.16)
     and R17 dissipating 2.86 W in place; the budget for the FETs and R17's coupling is 64.59 K
   R17's coupling into a junction is at most that FET's Zself (a passive network peaks where it is heated; reciprocity), so it is bounded with no layout
     known; designed apart it is held to 1 K/W, which E-1 reads
   the pair (Zself + Zmut)            3.027 W each: FETs only 21.34 K/W; R17 apart 20.39 K/W; R17 anywhere 10.96 K/W
   three (Zself + 2 Zmut)             1.345 W each: FETs only 48.01 K/W; R17 apart 45.88 K/W; R17 anywhere 15.34 K/W
   E11-29's target for the pair was 33.12 K/W (L4-E11's 19c withdraws it and restates E11-29 as this limit: 45.88 K/W a FET with R17 apart, 150 C held at
     23.93 A from 76.25 C); Ciss: the pair 4.72 nF at -15 V and 5.74 near 0 V, three 7.08 and about 8.61, against TI's 5 nF (L4-E11 16c, E11-37)
   SELECTED: a third BUK6Y10-30P (its designator L4-E11's: Q42 in its round 9 draft, not applied; Q41 is l8r2's VIN_RAW cut-off FET), R17 designed apart: the path asked is 1.39 times
